    "question": {
      "stem": "Why does the retry in `charge_with_retry` now reuse `original.key` instead of making a new `OperationKey`?",
      "options": {
        "A": "So that the provider treats the retry as the same charge, and a charge that went through before the timeout isn't made twice.",
        "B": "So that the retry skips the provider's checks on the card and completes faster than the first attempt.",
        "C": "So that the provider rejects the retry if the first attempt failed, and the caller sees the original timeout."
