      "criterion_1": {
        "statement": "Explains that a timed-out charge may still have gone through.",
        "met": "Says the first charge might have succeeded even though the client saw a timeout.",
        "not_met": "Treats the timeout as proof that nothing was charged, or doesn't consider it.",
        "outcome": "not met",
        "explanation": "Your reasoning explains what the key does but never says why a retry is risky in the first place: a timeout doesn't tell the client whether the first charge went through. The retry only happens in the `Err(Error::Timeout)` arm, so the first request may already have been processed by the provider before the client gave up. That uncertainty is the reason a fresh `OperationKey` could cause a second charge, and meeting this criterion means saying that the first charge might have succeeded despite the timeout.",
